// The calls of a file are filled from its own module's givens and the givens of its scopes; a given
// imported by name is read as a value, `current.id`, and passed by name, `tx = current`, but fills no
// call, so a call with no given of the type in the file's own scopes is an error.
// error: `tag` needs a `Tx` for `tx`, and no given of that type is in scope
import context
import context.{current}

main()
  println(current.id)
  println(context.tag(tx = current))
  println(context.tag())
